# kbd-toggle

A handy script to provide a virtual toggle switch for powering on and off
your laptop's built-in keyboard.

## usage

### install

To install the tool,

```shell
cd kbd-toggle && ./install.sh
```

To reverse the tool installation,

```shell
cd kbd-toggle && ./uninstall.sh
```

### activation

The end-user script is at `~/local/bin/toggle_keyboard.sh` and this can be
paired with a keyboard shortcut to toggle the laptop's built-in keyboard.

